<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 40,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>These are for January shipment. The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000	   Western white	    25,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   20,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				    (13 percent protein)  20,000</p>
<p>				    (Ordinary)		15,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  40,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Standard white	   40,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>				   Food			 20,000</p>
</text>
